WEBVTT

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.120
Come home.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.650
You know you can't stay here.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.920
No!

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.610
I'm... not ready.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.240
How long are you going 
to act like a child?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.480
You just stopped answering my calls, 
and then you came all the way out here.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.600
What if somebody with
bad intentions took you in?

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.740
Well...

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.210
Yoshida-san is a good person.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.930
Sayu, adults aren't like kids. They can
 pretend to be good people all they want.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.800
Yoshida-san isn't like that!

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.020
Don't try to use him against me!

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.690
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.870
"Past"

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.320
Sorry about that. I took the day off work, 
so I can hear all you have to say.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.980
Thank you.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.320
Let me start with this.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.170
Has anything inappropriate 
happened between you two?

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.670
No.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.670
Absolutely not!

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.900
I see.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:39.180
So let me thank you for taking her in.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.180
No...

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.670
I was worried about the environment 
she'd found herself in.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.180
I can imagine.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.710
Sayu, Mother is worried.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.860
You're lying! 
Mom would never worry about me!

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.110
She's looking for you, if nothing else.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.930
That woman would never do 
something like that!

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.120
Tell me the real reason.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:11.520
Your teacher's come looking for you 
several times since you left.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.080
She doesn't want any incidents,

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.950
so she's told him you've locked
yourself inside your room.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.840
It seems that the school now thinks 
she may be locking you in there.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.680
And she wants me to go back 
to prove them wrong?

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.890
Then what she's worried about 
is what people will say.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.610
Not Sayu's feelings?

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.810
I don't believe so.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.570
But I can't say definitely 
that she's put much thought into it at all.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.750
Once our mother gets an idea, 
she doesn't give it up.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.930
It will be difficult for you 
to continue to run.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.250
Can we have a few days, at least?

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.000
A few days?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.440
Just a few.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.960
Is that possible?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.480
It seems to me 
that Sayu needs time to think.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.140
Would you let me talk to Sayu 
for a moment, alone?

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.630
I promise I won't take her away.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.300
All right.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.330
Is that okay with you too, Sayu?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:19.900
Yeah.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.080
I'm sorry.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.820
This must've surprised you, right?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.290
I'm sure it was a shock to you, too.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.130
I thought that you'd get to go home 
when you were ready.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.370
That it was your choice.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:36.860
Yeah.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.610
But we found out it's not that simple.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.480
Yoshida-san!

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:45.740
What's wrong?

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.090
I'm a little scared.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.830
I thought I had to go back someday,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.740
but now that the day's finally here,

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.550
I realize how weak I am.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.650
I'm scared, too.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.610
So don't worry.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:09.220
Yoshida-san, when I'm with you, 
I feel relaxed.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.640
Thank you. I'll go talk with my brother.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.340
Okay, good luck!

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.470
<i>It's a good thing!</i>

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.430
<i>I was hoping Sayu'd go back, anyway.</i>

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:37.640
<i>But now...</i>

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:46.860
There aren't many adults out there who'd
take in another's child out of pure goodwill.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:49.700
Yeah.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.120
I was worried about 
what might've happened to you.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.290
But I feel a little better.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.940
He seems really worried about you, huh?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:01.900
Yeah.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:10.200
Mother calls and asks if I found you.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.760
Every single day.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.060
I see.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:17.880
After what happened, she's been unstable.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.500
It's been worse since you left.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.730
So you should go back, for now.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.630
I'll help you all I can.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:31.950
At first, I ran because it was painful.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:36.380
But that was true no matter where I went.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.910
I realized I was alone 
no matter where I went.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.070
And then I met Yoshida-san.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.510
He taught me how stupid I'd been.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:51.090
About how important the things 
I lost coming here were.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.710
So I told myself that I needed to start 
thinking for myself about what I want to be.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:05.070
Until I know what I'm going to take back home 
with me, after coming all this way,

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.780
I don't want to go home.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.350
I see.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.960
You've changed a little, too.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.370
You speak your mind more than you did before.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.370
Yeah. You may be right.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:33.300
I can buy you a week at most—
convince her that I just haven't found you yet.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:35.000
Do you mean...?

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:39.730
I mean, "Take a week to think."

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.420
Thank you.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>Today</b>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>You up?</b>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>Yeah.</b>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>What is it?</b>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>Can you come to Yoshida-san's house ASAP? 
I need to talk to you.</b>

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>Got it.</b>

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>I'll be there in 30.</b>

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.400
<b>Thanks</b>

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:04.570
I see. So you've gotta
head back in a week, huh?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:05.420
Yeah.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:09.100
Man, I'm gonna miss you.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:14.470
Your brother gave your decision more
respect than I thought he would.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.470
I guess so.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:20.150
You've got a week. 
You need to use it to think.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.640
Yeah.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:28.310
So I want to tell you 
what's happened to me until now.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:32.190
Okay. My friend's facing her past.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.190
I need to support her, 
or I'm not a real friend.

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.110
Yeah...

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.280
Are you nervous, Yoshida-cchi?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.080
Shut up!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.260
Okay, I'll tell you, then.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:49.560
I never got along with my mother.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.470
And that was one of the reasons that, 
when I got to high school,

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:56.200
I never really wanted 
to put effort into anything.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.760
Not my schoolwork, 
not hanging out with friends...

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.940
I didn't care about any of it.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.030
Everyone else avoided me, 
and that was fine.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.260
But...

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.650
Sayu-chan, can I eat lunch with you?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.590
Okay, I guess...

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.990
Um, what is it, Yuuko?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:24.650
You look really cool in profile.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.880
What the heck?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.630
Why are you so cool?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.210
"Why"?

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:36.810
Yuuko was like me. She didn't fit in.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:41.740
To the others, I'm sure it just looked like 
two class rejects hanging out.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.470
But I really enjoyed being with Yuuko.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:51.820
You look your best 
when you're smiling, Sayu-chan.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.660
Because of her, I started to smile.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:58.740
But...

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:03.700
<b>Math II</b>

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.700
Yuuko started being bullied 
by a group of girls.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.110
You okay?

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.570
Yeah.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.300
But why is this happening to you?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.590
Yuuko?

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:29.480
Sayu-chan, one of the guys on the basketball team 
asked you out, and you rejected him, right?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.450
Y-Yeah...

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:36.420
One of them likes him. I think that's why.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:41.030
But wouldn't they go after me then?

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:48.370
Well... you have a pretty face. You're cool.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.940
Sayu-chan, you just don't look like a bad person.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.760
No matter what lies they tell about you,

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.980
they can't get everybody to hate you.

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:01.050
So they went after you instead?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.310
But it's fine.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:07.060
I'm gloomy. I'm not pretty at all.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:10.980
It's weird for me to be hanging out with you.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:13.450
Yuuko...

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:16.700
They said I was like your groupie.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.820
But they're not wrong.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.150
That's not true!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:26.090
Yuuko, you're my first friend!

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.650
Here.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.600
My friend was being bullied because of me.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.370
And I didn't even realize it.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.720
It made me sick.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.690
I'm sure she's got the idea by now.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:54.920
Right?

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:58.860
Little Miss Princess needs to choose
better friends, don't you think?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.110
Right?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:05.160
I bet she thinks hanging out with the girl 
with no friends makes the boys like her more.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.410
Yuuko!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.140
Sayu-chan!

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.440
I'll never betray you. 
So let's fight together!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.620
Sayu-chan!

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.820
I thought we'd be okay, together.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.470
That we couldn't lose.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.920
But looking back, 
I think I'd made a big mistake.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.430
Wh-What are you doing, Yuuko?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.720
Sayu-chan.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:15.340
Th-That's really dangerous. 
Come back...

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.480
I've been waiting for you here.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:26.100
When I first saw you, 
I thought you were really pretty.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:30.440
Solitary, beautiful... 
Keeping everyone away.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.060
What are you talking about?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:37.100
But I'm not very smart, 
so I got close to you anyway.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:42.410
And when I talked to you, 
you were just an ordinary, cute girl.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:47.430
Kind, caring, with a wonderful smile.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.830
And I ruined that.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:56.060
I turned the solitary and beautiful Sayu-chan

00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:00.710
into a stupid girl who hangs
out with a loser like me.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.040
You're not like me!

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:06.070
You can shine brighter!

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.260
And I—

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:11.780
the person who admires you most—

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.360
I ruined it.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.810
Did you know you've stopped
laughing altogether lately?

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:26.190
All you think about is protecting me. 
You always look so depressed.

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:29.010
O-Of course! You're my friend!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.030
Thank you.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:36.010
But you know, 
that hurt me more than anything.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.820
This isn't your fault, you know.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.040
Yuuko?

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.990
So keep on smiling, okay?

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.470
Are you home?

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:31.430
Ogiwara-san, are you there?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:36.260
Leave us alone! 
I told you we have nothing to do with it!

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.520
Ogiwara-san, wait!

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.030
Ogiwara-san, just answer a few questions!

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.310
Mom...

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.850
This is all your fault!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.560
Stop making my life harder, damn it!

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:09.320
I'm sorry.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:13.320
Why are they mad at us 
about somebody else's suicide?

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.990
Issa's working so hard, but all you do is...

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.360
I'm sorry.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:26.230
Don't tell me. 
You didn't kill her, did you?

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.140
Shut the hell up.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:39.220
Of course I didn't!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.230
You'll never understand!

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:46.960
My best friend was bullied 
because of me, and she died!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.940
You'll never understand how that feels!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.580
If I bother you that much, I'll just leave.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.870
Sayu, is it okay for you to leave the house?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.750
Sayu!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.500
Let me go!

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:08.020
I'm done with this place!

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:09.470
Calm down.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.940
What happened?

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.510
Mom asked me...

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:18.930
if I killed Yuuko!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.900
She did what?

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:31.370
I understand. You should probably 
get some distance from Mother.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.120
Goodbye.

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.580
Sayu, take this.

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.040
There's 300,000 yen inside.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.850
If you don't go on a spending spree, 
it'll last you two weeks.

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.420
I can't take that.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.380
And I can't have you running away 
without any money.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:55.200
Listen. You need to stay in a real hotel.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:18:00.680
And contact me if you feel you're in danger.

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.850
If you can promise me those two things,

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.820
I can keep Mother from finding out.

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.370
Thank you.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.560
You've been through a lot.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.220
Get some rest.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.150
Okay.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:24.160
I ran away from my mom and was finally free,

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.340
but I never felt any better.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.080
All I felt was loneliness.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:35.110
At some point, the money
my brother gave me ran out.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:38.950
And then the emptiness and
the feelings of worthlessness crept in.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:43.750
Even his kindness started 
to feel like pity to me.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.510
<b>Ogiwara Issa</b>

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:49.940
In the end, I didn't mean anything to anyone.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:55.900
By the time I realized that, 
even I was surprised at how much I didn't care.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:59.030
And then...

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.160
Hey, what's a girl your age 
doing out at this hour?

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.410
I ran away from home.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.310
I don't have anywhere to go.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.840
Fine. It's dangerous to be out here alone.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:15.020
You can stay with me tonight.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.200
It's not a bother?

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.000
At first, I didn't even realize I'd said it.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:25.480
And that's how it started.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.910
At first, I thought maybe he was letting
me stay out of the goodness of his heart.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.810
But after a few days, he wanted sex.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:39.780
And since I didn't want
to go home, I gave in.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:43.750
I'm really stupid, huh?

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.630
I don't even remember the name 
of the guy I was with my first time.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:48.920
Sayu-chan...

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:51.690
And you know the rest.

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:55.110
Once it started, I just kept going.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.330
Sex for a place to stay.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.340
I kept that up...

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:03.430
until I met Yoshida-san.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:09.980
That's everything that happened to me 
after I left Hokkaido until I met Yoshida-san.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.920
I see...

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.210
Thanks for telling me.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:20.500
Sayu-chan, you really
hung in there, didn't you?

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.080
Yeah...

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.240
You really did, huh?

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:31.110
Yeah, I did.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.940
I really did.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.040
She calmed down.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.510
I see.

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:53.320
I knew there was something,

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.550
but I didn't think it'd be this bad.

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:57.820
Yeah.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.730
Her friend committed suicide,

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:03.040
and her mom, who should've been more
supportive than anybody, blamed her instead.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:04.890
Even an adult couldn't handle that.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:08.730
So, what will you do?

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.330
About what?

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:12.760
About Sayu-chaso.

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:15.710
Just let her go home?

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.910
Her family's come to get her.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.680
I'm a stranger. I can't do a thing.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:26.130
A stranger? After all that's happened?

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:29.220
This is a problem for her family to solve.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.800
Who knows if her family's even on her side?!

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:34.680
What do you want to do, Yoshida-cchi?

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.720
Were you listening?

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.650
It's not my place to get involved.

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:41.130
That's not what I'm asking.

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:43.860
I'm not asking what your "place" is!

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.320
I'm asking what you want to do about her.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:50.870
What I...

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:57.530
...want to do?

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
"Proof"

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Watch next week, okay?</b>
